suant to new statutory authority and recent appropriations providing $8 million to extend Head Start eligibility and services in the Freely Associated States, as authorized under the Compacts of Free Association Amendments Act of 2024 (Division","agencies":["Health and Human Services Department","Children and Families Administration"]},{"title":"Commercial Driver's License: State of Hawaii Department of Transportation; Application for Exemption","type":"Notice","date":"2026-05-14","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/05/14/2026-09622/commercial-drivers-license-state-of-hawaii-department-of-transportation-application-for-exemption","abstract":"FMCSA announces its decision to grant in part and deny in part the exemption application from the Hawaii Department of Transportation (HDOT). FMCSA grants all State Driver's Licensing Agencies (SDLAs) a five-year exemption to issue a non-domiciled commercial driver's license (CDL) or non-domiciled commercial learner's permit (CLP) to citizens of Freely Associated States (FAS) who reside in the United States and who have a valid, unexpired passport issued by an FAS and a Form I-94 or I -94A. The FAS are the Federated States of Micronesia, the Republic of the Marshall Islands, and the Republic o","agencies":["Transportation Department","Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration"]},{"title":"Clarification of Deposit Insurance Coverage for Branches of U.S. Banks in the Federated States of Micronesia, the Marshall Islands, and Palau","type":"Rule","date":"2026-03-23","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/03/23/2026-05652/clarification-of-deposit-insurance-coverage-for-branches-of-us-banks-in-the-federated-states-of","abstract":"The Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) is adopting a final rule to provide that the FDIC will insure deposits of all branches of U.S.-insured depository institutions (IDIs) in the Federated States of Micronesia, the Republic of the Marshall Islands, and the Republic of Palau, whether operating presently or in the future. This final rule follows an interim final rule with request for comment issued by the FDIC in August 2024.","agencies":["Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation"]},{"title":"Delegation of Authority Under Section 208(d)(6) of the Compact of Free Association Amendments Act of 2024","type":"Presidential Document","date":"2025-12-19","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/12/19/2025-23568/delegation-of-authority-under-section-208d6-of-the-compact-of-free-association-amendments-act-of","abstract":"","agencies":["Executive Office of the President"]},{"title":"Fiscal Year (FY) 2025 Notice of Supplemental Funding Opportunity","type":"Notice","date":"2025-08-25","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/08/25/2025-16259/fiscal-year-fy-2025-notice-of-supplemental-funding-opportunity","abstract":"This notice is to inform the public that the Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration (SAMHSA) is supporting administrative supplements in scope of the parent award for the 58 eligible grant recipients funded in FY 2025 under the State Opioid Response (SOR), Notice of Funding Opportunity (NOFO) TI-24-008. The SOR formula will be used to calculate the award amounts for all 50 states, District of Columbia and Puerto Rico with a minimum award constraint of $500,000. The following six territories: American Samoa, Guam, Micronesia, Northern Mariana Islands, Palau, and Virgin Island","agencies":["Health and Human Services Department","Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services Administration"]},{"title":"Solicitation of Nominations for Appointment to the Advisory Committee on United States Outlying Areas and Freely Associated States","type":"Notice","date":"2025-08-08","url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/08/08/2025-15104/solicitation-of-nominations-for-appointment-to-the-advisory-committee-on-united-states-outlying","abstract":"The Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Veteran